Scan the source files under each path with the active rules of the ruleset.
The default path is the current directory.
The exit status is 1 when a finding has the --fail-level severity or a higher severity.

Usage:
  semscope scan [paths...] [flags]

Flags:
      --disable-rule strings   the same as --omit-rule
      --enable-rule strings    enable the rules with these IDs
      --exclude stringArray    skip the paths that match this path.Match pattern, relative to the scan root; repeat the flag to add patterns
      --fail-level string      the lowest severity that gives exit status 1: error, warning, note or none (default "error")
      --format string          the output format: text, json or sarif (default "text")
  -h, --help                   help for scan
      --omit-rule strings      omit the rules with these IDs
  -o, --output string          the output file (default stdout)
  -r, --ruleset stringArray    a built-in ruleset, a .cue file or a directory; repeat the flag to add overlays (default nasa-p10)
      --sarif-version string   the SARIF version: 2.1.0, or 2.2 (an OASIS draft) (default "2.1.0")
      --set stringArray        override a rule parameter: RULE_ID.param=value (a list value is comma-separated)
